Falsifies `page_frames::verification::mark_free_frees_only_whole_frames_inside_the_range`.

The defect: `mark_free` walks `page_frame_range`, the outward-rounding range `mark_used` needs,
in place of `whole_frames_in`. Both return a `Range<usize>` of frame indices from the same
arguments, so the type system cannot tell them apart.

Expected to fail: both of the harness's assertions. A range starting partway into a frame frees
that frame, which begins below `start`; a range ending partway into a frame frees that frame,
which ends past `start + size`. That is a frame only partly inside a usable region becoming
allocatable.

